    <div class="prose">
      <p>Nobody wakes up wanting new windows. They notice the draught, the condensation, the tired old front door letting the house down, and eventually they start looking. The job is worth thousands, so they're not impulse buyers, they're comparing. That's fine. It just means you need to be one of the names they see and trust while they're deciding.</p>

      <h2>What the ads bring in</h2>
      <p>I target homeowners, and the ads are built around the jobs that pay:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Full window replacements, uPVC and composite</li>
        <li>Composite and uPVC front and back doors</li>
        <li>Patio, French and bi-fold doors</li>
        <li>Single rooms or full-house replacements</li>
      </ul>

      <div class="split">
        <div class="prose" style="margin:0;">
          <h2>Why real footage matters here</h2>
          <p>A homeowner spending thousands wants to see real, finished work, not a stock photo of a window every other fitter is using too. So we use <strong>real footage of your installs</strong>, filmed on site or from jobs you've already done. It shows the standard of your finish and builds trust before they've even messaged, which matters a lot when the job's this size.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <figure style="max-width:300px;margin:0 auto;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:14px;overflow:hidden;background:#14110c;">
            <video style="width:100%;display:block;" controls muted playsinline preload="none" poster="/clips/MGUPVC_Showcase.jpg" aria-label="Window and door installation ad footage">
              <source src="/clips/MGUPVC_Showcase.mp4" type="video/mp4">
            </video>
